<title>USA: DBS Industries closes merger.</title>
<headline>DBS Industries closes merger.</headline>
<dateline>MILL VALLEY, Calif. 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>DBS Industries Inc said Friday it closed the merger between EchoStar Communications Corp and Direct Broadcasting Satellite Corp, 24.8 percent owned by DBS Industries.</p>
<p>In exchange for its ownership in DBSC, DBS Industries will receive 270,414 Class A Common Shares of EchoStar stock, a statement from DBS Industries said.</p>
<p>EchoStar common stock closed at $25.00 on January 8, valuing the deal at $6.7 Million, the statement said.</p>
<p>The merger is intended to further strengthen EchoStar's competitive position within the direct-to-home satellite market, the statement said.</p>
